{
  "requirement": "The `TypeScript` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct TypeScript;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for TypeScript;\nimpl Debug for TypeScript;\nimpl Default for TypeScript;\nimpl OutlineLang for TypeScript;\nimpl Copy for TypeScript;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.sources.typescript.TypeScript` requires a unit struct `TypeScript` with `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy`. It also requires that the `OutlineLang` implementation supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules. The detailed rules belong to the refining requirements `requirements.sdk.sources.typescript.language`, `requirements.sdk.sources.typescript.fingerprints` and `requirements.sdk.sources.typescript.items`. Those rules are assessed through their own tests, not here.\n\nTest coverage:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` calls its inner `check` helper with `languages::TypeScript`.\n  - The helper's `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy` bound makes `TypeScript` implement `OutlineLang`, `Default` and `Copy`, and the call compiles.\n  - It asserts `extensions()` equals `[\"ts\",\"mts\",\"cts\"]`, with uppercase filenames also resolving to the language.\n  - It asserts `fingerprint_scheme()` equals `typescript-structural-v2`, and that `L::default()` has the same scheme.\n  - It asserts `size_of` is 0, so `TypeScript` is a unit struct.\n  - It checks `Clone::clone`, and that the clone reports the same extensions.\n  - It checks that `outline()` and `from_source_with` agree with the inferred outline. The root span covers the whole source, `select(\"function[check]\")` succeeds, and the fingerprints match.\n  - It checks that `search_structure` returns valid ranges.\n- `typescript_and_tsx_share_signatures_abstract_classes_and_module_kinds` checks TypeScript outline selection on a richer source. It covers generators, declared signatures, abstract classes, and ambient modules and namespaces.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that the public export inventory matches the appendix. It also checks that the Habeas consumer compiles against the SDK.\n\nNo test asserts `Debug` output. `Debug` is generated by the `language!` macro, so it is a plain derive with no conditional or transformation of its own. The public export test also compiles against the documented trait list. I treat this as covered, and I found no behavior a reviewer could reasonably call untested.",
  "references": "0355d17c38a7af5dbeca90004bc00a58d9249f1fe4e8fe43b137760bcdb227a1",
